    "product_faq_tPH4tG": {
      "type": "Product-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "left_U8xBjD": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I’m using a hormonal contraceptive",
            "dsc1": "<p>While you can certainly take Monthlies powder for its potential benefits, it's important to note that hormonal contraceptives, such as implants and pills, can affect hormone levels.  </p><p>Since hormonal contraceptives regulate your hormone balance, the efficacy of the powder might be compromised by the contraceptive method you are using.</p>"
          }
        },
        "left_78AnJL": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I’m on a fertility treatment",
            "dsc1": "<p>Fertility treatments often involve precise hormone manipulation.</p><p>It's vital to recognise that introducing new supplements, including the Monthlies powder, should be done under the guidance of your healthcare provider. The introduction of external supplements could potentially disrupt the intended hormonal adjustments of the treatment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "left_4BR8xr": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I’m already taking supplements",
            "dsc1": "<p>If you're currently using any medication or have been prescribed supplements for specific vitamin deficiencies, it's essential to consult your healthcare provider before incorporating Monthlies into your daily regimen.  </p><p>The Monthlies powder blend is designed to provide a fundamental level of hormone support, aiming to fulfil your body's requirements. This implies that you might not need to acquire extra vitamin and mineral supplements to address foundational hormone balance needs.</p>"
          }
        },
        "right_Bt4xyP": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "I have PCOS",
            "dsc": "<p>PCOS is a reproductive disorder characterised by the presence of cysts on the ovaries, elevated testosterone levels, and irregular periods. To be diagnosed with PCOS, a patient must exhibit at least 2 out of these 3 symptoms. However, several other symptoms are commonly associated with PCOS, including insulin resistance, difficulty losing weight, excess hair growth, hair loss, and depression.</p><p>If you're diagnosed with PCOS, then you're probably in more pain than our natural solutions can soothe all by themselves.</p><p>However, the blend of ingredients aims to support overall hormone balance, potentially benefiting those with endometriosis. <strong>It's advisable to consult our experts to determine the best approach for your unique needs.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "right_L8j6xV": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "I have endometriosis",
            "dsc": "<p>Endometriosis is a medical condition that occurs when tissue resembling the uterine lining grows outside the womb, often in areas such as the ovaries or fallopian tubes. This condition can cause intense pain during a woman's menstrual cycle and, for some, even when they're not menstruating.</p><p>Diagnosis of endometriosis can be challenging, resulting in an average duration of 6-10 years before receiving an accurate diagnosis.</p><p>If you're diagnosed with endometriosis, then you're probably in more pain than our natural solutions can soothe all by themselves.</p><p>However, the blend of ingredients aims to support overall hormone balance, potentially benefiting those with endometriosis. <strong>It's advisable to consult our experts to determine the best  approach for your unique needs.</strong></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "left_U8xBjD",
